## 3.  Switching back to CPU

If you want to run the same code on the CPU, just change the policy:

```cpp
// Replace
RAJA::forall<RAJA::cuda_exec<256, RAJA::cuda_async>>(...)

// With
RAJA::forall<RAJA::omp_parallel_for_exec>(...)
```

or

```cpp
RAJA::kernel<RAJA::omp_parallel_for_exec>(...)
```

The rest of the code stays identical. This is the essence of RAJA’s portability: the *policy* decides where the loop runs, while the *loop body* stays the same.

